        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "GEN. NOEL J. FRANCISCO, Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioners"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Masterpiece Cakeshop, Ltd. (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. WAGGONER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The First Amendment prohibits the government from forcing people to express messages that their violate religious convictions. Yet the Commission requires Mr. Phillips to do just that, ordering him to sketch, sculpt, and hand-paint cakes that celebrate a view of marriage in violation of his religious convictions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Can I ask you -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument this morning in Case 16-111, Masterpiece Cakeshop versus Colorado Civil Rights Commission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, actually, counsel, that seems to be a point of contention. The state seems to concede that if it were the message, your -- your client would have a right to refuse. But if it -- the objection is to the person, that's when the discrimination law kicks in. That's Footnote 8 of the Colorado Court of Appeals' decision. I know you know this.\nSo what do you say to that, that actually what is happening here may superficially look like it's about the message, but it's really about the person's identity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF GEN. NOEL J. FRANCISCO ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: If you prevail, could the baker put a sign in his window, we do not bake cakes for gay weddings?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State Respondent",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the question is going to be is -- is that operating in the sense of a retail store? If it is, then, yes, a state can require a -\u00ad someone offering a service to give the same services regardless of -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What facts do you need besides the ones I've given you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But you'd agree that would be a problem -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: You have five -- five more minutes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Yarger",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YARGER: He -- a training requirement is a common remedy that's used in many civil rights cases. He -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bob Jones University",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Bob Jones University said we're not discriminating on the basis of race; we allow black people to come into the school. We just refuse to admit those who are engaged in interracial marriages or advocate interracial dating."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8413c34f1ba9c25aff4c494c89d004378570d90c4ca6f4439dc2f76d26d0db02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8413c34f1ba9-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Is your -- is your answer to my hypothetical about the religious legal services organization the same as Mr. Yarger's?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-111",
